1
00:01:00,945 --> 00:01:03,585
<i>You threw away my ring, didn't you?</i>

2
00:01:03,665 --> 00:01:04,984
So that ring matters more than me?

3
00:01:05,064 --> 00:01:06,465
<i>You fell for your mother's trick.</i>

4
00:01:06,545 --> 00:01:08,065
This was your plan, wasn't it?

5
00:01:08,145 --> 00:01:10,025
I'd never scheme against you.

6
00:01:10,105 --> 00:01:12,065
You're so full of it!

7
00:01:12,145 --> 00:01:15,305
-Huh?
-That's enough. Mom! Stop it!

8
00:01:16,425 --> 00:01:19,625
I'm Gingkamol, Runchlaphat's mother.
A show, you say?

9
00:01:20,305 --> 00:01:21,985
I just want her to know that

10
00:01:23,625 --> 00:01:25,345
loving someone

11
00:01:26,665 --> 00:01:29,385
shouldn't come at the cost of breaking

12
00:01:29,465 --> 00:01:31,145
a mother's heart.

13
00:01:31,745 --> 00:01:35,745
Guys, have you seen
<i>Real Talk With Moms</i> yet?

14
00:01:35,825 --> 00:01:37,785
Oh. I only saw bits of it.

15
00:01:37,865 --> 00:01:40,105
Our boss's mother was on it, right?

16
00:01:40,745 --> 00:01:45,025
Yeah. I tell you, this is a big deal.

17
00:01:46,905 --> 00:01:49,865
Hey. I think what she said
was great, though.

18
00:01:49,945 --> 00:01:52,185
She seemed like a very open-minded mother.

19
00:01:53,385 --> 00:01:55,505
That's why it's shady.

20
00:01:56,025 --> 00:01:59,065
Smart people imply things
instead of being direct,

21
00:01:59,145 --> 00:02:01,145
leaving the audience to figure it out.

22
00:02:02,785 --> 00:02:06,025
"Some people use love to gain control,

23
00:02:07,025 --> 00:02:08,584
not to understand."

24
00:02:09,345 --> 00:02:11,625
Our boss's mother said it herself.

25
00:02:12,625 --> 00:02:13,985
Who does that remind you of?

26
00:02:20,105 --> 00:02:21,785
You don't have to answer that.

27
00:02:21,865 --> 00:02:23,705
But just look at the comments.

28
00:02:23,785 --> 00:02:25,225
The whole country knows.

29
00:02:25,305 --> 00:02:28,385
It's their family's business, though.

30
00:02:28,465 --> 00:02:29,785
You could say that.

31
00:02:29,865 --> 00:02:32,345
But for someone like her,
it stops being a private matter.

32
00:02:32,425 --> 00:02:34,385
Our boss chose her wife

33
00:02:34,465 --> 00:02:37,105
and let her mother go on the show and cry.

34
00:02:39,145 --> 00:02:41,345
If it were me,
of course I'd choose my mother.

35
00:02:41,425 --> 00:02:42,745
You only have one mother, after all.

36
00:02:43,985 --> 00:02:44,865
Am I right?

37
00:02:54,185 --> 00:02:55,265
Runch!

38
00:02:55,865 --> 00:02:57,105
Morning.

39
00:02:57,185 --> 00:03:00,545
I took a beach trip,
so I bought you some desserts.

40
00:03:00,625 --> 00:03:03,665
I'll leave them in the coffee room

41
00:03:03,745 --> 00:03:05,505
so everyone can enjoy them.

42
00:03:06,665 --> 00:03:08,545
Runch, wait.

43
00:03:09,945 --> 00:03:11,705
You shouldn't go in there yet.

44
00:03:12,465 --> 00:03:13,505
Why not?

45
00:03:16,945 --> 00:03:20,345
Some people, huh? When they're in love,

46
00:03:20,425 --> 00:03:22,505
they forget everything else,

47
00:03:22,585 --> 00:03:24,625
even those who raised them.

48
00:03:28,785 --> 00:03:29,945
What?

49
00:03:30,665 --> 00:03:32,985
I just feel bad for her mother.

50
00:03:33,065 --> 00:03:35,505
A good person like her is hurt

51
00:03:35,585 --> 00:03:36,865
because her daughter
chose the wrong person.

52
00:03:39,585 --> 00:03:41,305
Are you done, Utt?

53
00:03:51,185 --> 00:03:52,825
You don't know me

54
00:03:52,905 --> 00:03:55,505
or the relationship I have with my mother.

55
00:03:55,585 --> 00:03:58,665
You have no right to criticize me
over my private life.

56
00:03:58,745 --> 00:04:00,265
Why not, Boss?

57
00:04:01,185 --> 00:04:03,385
I'm just repeating what I heard.

58
00:04:04,145 --> 00:04:05,825
Your mother said it herself.

59
00:04:06,345 --> 00:04:07,945
Everybody who heard her could tell

60
00:04:08,545 --> 00:04:11,065
that you chose your wife over your mother.

61
00:04:12,145 --> 00:04:14,425
Or did I get it wrong?

62
00:04:14,505 --> 00:04:16,545
If you say another word,

63
00:04:17,225 --> 00:04:19,545
I'll sue you for defamation.

64
00:04:25,665 --> 00:04:27,585
It's time to work.

65
00:04:27,665 --> 00:04:30,345
I hope you can do your job as well

66
00:04:31,185 --> 00:04:33,545
as you gossip.

67
00:04:38,465 --> 00:04:39,625
Next time,

68
00:04:41,065 --> 00:04:42,665
if you want to talk about me,

69
00:04:43,265 --> 00:04:45,985
why don't you say it to my face?

70
00:05:10,505 --> 00:05:13,505
Runch, Are you okay?

71
00:05:16,785 --> 00:05:18,025
I'm okay.

72
00:05:20,105 --> 00:05:22,185
What's wrong with Utt?

73
00:05:22,265 --> 00:05:24,505
He's acted this way many times.

74
00:05:24,585 --> 00:05:26,865
He doesn't seem to like you very much,

75
00:05:26,945 --> 00:05:30,185
even though you're his boss.

76
00:05:33,105 --> 00:05:35,425
I never cared to find out why.

77
00:05:37,305 --> 00:05:39,785
He's nobody important to me.

78
00:05:39,865 --> 00:05:42,825
Whatever he thinks, says, or does,

79
00:05:42,905 --> 00:05:44,385
let's just let him be.

80
00:05:48,985 --> 00:05:51,385
Hey, Utt. Calm down. Don't be so mad.

81
00:05:51,465 --> 00:05:53,425
-I hate her.
-You're doing too much.

82
00:05:53,505 --> 00:05:55,425
I'm not. I don't like her.

83
00:05:55,505 --> 00:05:57,825
I haven't for a while now.
I just can't stand her.

84
00:05:57,905 --> 00:05:58,865
What's wrong with you?

85
00:05:58,945 --> 00:06:02,265
She never did anything to you.
You always started it.

86
00:06:02,345 --> 00:06:04,025
Mind your own business!

87
00:06:04,105 --> 00:06:07,665
Hey, Utt. If you keep taking it out on me,
I'm done talking to you.

88
00:07:08,425 --> 00:07:11,785
You freaks… One day I'll get you back.

89
00:07:18,785 --> 00:07:20,065
Sorry,

90
00:07:20,145 --> 00:07:21,825
Ms. Peeracha isn't available
for an interview.

91
00:07:21,905 --> 00:07:25,065
If you have any concerns,
please send us an email.

92
00:07:27,905 --> 00:07:30,825
Yes. But we'd rather not comment on that.

93
00:07:30,905 --> 00:07:32,225
Thank you.

94
00:07:34,785 --> 00:07:35,665
Sorry,

95
00:07:35,745 --> 00:07:39,025
Ms. Peeracha has no plans
to speak to the media.

96
00:07:41,425 --> 00:07:44,265
What happened?
Why are they calling us nonstop?

97
00:07:44,985 --> 00:07:48,825
It's the press, Ms. Neen. Reporters
and online content creators.

98
00:07:48,905 --> 00:07:50,385
From so many agencies too.

99
00:07:50,985 --> 00:07:51,985
The media?

100
00:07:53,225 --> 00:07:54,425
But why?

101
00:07:55,025 --> 00:07:55,985
Well…

102
00:07:56,865 --> 00:07:59,225
It's about Mrs. Gingkamol
being on that show.

103
00:07:59,825 --> 00:08:03,385
They wanted to interview you about…

104
00:08:04,905 --> 00:08:07,545
your family's relationship.

105
00:08:13,985 --> 00:08:15,505
Are you okay, Neen?

106
00:08:18,105 --> 00:08:20,265
I'm okay.

107
00:08:20,345 --> 00:08:22,625
It's chaos over here, though.

108
00:08:22,705 --> 00:08:24,825
The press won't stop calling.

109
00:08:26,185 --> 00:08:28,385
They're calling you?

110
00:08:28,465 --> 00:08:32,784
Yeah. They want to interview me
about your mother being on that show.

111
00:08:35,065 --> 00:08:36,985
I didn't think

112
00:08:37,065 --> 00:08:39,625
this would cause so much trouble for you.

113
00:08:39,705 --> 00:08:41,465
<i>It's a really big deal, though.</i>

114
00:08:41,545 --> 00:08:43,664
It's like everybody's so ready to judge us

115
00:08:43,745 --> 00:08:45,865
without knowing the full story.

116
00:08:47,425 --> 00:08:50,065
I'm really upset about what she did.

117
00:08:50,145 --> 00:08:52,465
No matter how hurt or sad she is,

118
00:08:53,065 --> 00:08:55,945
she has no right to tell anyone
about our private matters

119
00:08:56,025 --> 00:08:58,785
<i>and cause you trouble as a result.</i>

120
00:08:58,865 --> 00:09:00,545
I'm sorry.

121
00:09:02,265 --> 00:09:03,265
<i>It's okay.</i>

122
00:09:03,345 --> 00:09:06,825
I'm happy to hear
that you're siding with me.

123
00:09:07,425 --> 00:09:08,865
Well, I'm not happy at all.

124
00:09:15,425 --> 00:09:17,065
Oh, Runch.

125
00:09:17,585 --> 00:09:19,465
Why didn't you tell me you were coming?

126
00:09:19,545 --> 00:09:21,545
I would've made you dinner.

127
00:09:21,625 --> 00:09:23,225
Why did you do it?

128
00:09:24,105 --> 00:09:25,265
What did I do?

129
00:09:25,865 --> 00:09:29,265
You went on that show
and said all those things.

130
00:09:29,785 --> 00:09:31,745
I didn't do anything, Runch.

131
00:09:31,825 --> 00:09:35,185
They wanted me on the show
for an interview, so I said yes.

132
00:09:35,265 --> 00:09:37,305
It's not like I begged them to go.

133
00:09:37,385 --> 00:09:39,825
Didn't you think there'd be consequences?

134
00:09:41,025 --> 00:09:43,105
I simply said how I felt.

135
00:09:43,185 --> 00:09:45,465
I didn't slander your wife.

136
00:09:45,545 --> 00:09:48,385
I didn't even mention her name once.

137
00:09:49,185 --> 00:09:51,865
People just took it the wrong way.

138
00:09:51,945 --> 00:09:53,785
Well, your words

139
00:09:53,865 --> 00:09:56,105
made the whole country see it that way.

140
00:09:56,185 --> 00:09:57,025
See what?

141
00:09:57,105 --> 00:10:00,545
That Neen's the one
who took me away from you.

142
00:10:03,385 --> 00:10:06,225
-Or will you deny it?
-I never said that.

143
00:10:06,305 --> 00:10:08,425
But you knew full well

144
00:10:08,945 --> 00:10:11,505
how the viewers would think.

145
00:10:12,265 --> 00:10:15,305
Runch. I'm a mother.

146
00:10:15,385 --> 00:10:17,865
I have the right to express
my feelings as a mother.

147
00:10:18,785 --> 00:10:22,465
I was hurt. I was sad.

148
00:10:22,545 --> 00:10:24,345
So I gave them my side of the story.

149
00:10:24,425 --> 00:10:26,505
What about Neen's side?

150
00:10:29,985 --> 00:10:32,225
Neen never said anything.

151
00:10:32,305 --> 00:10:33,865
She never defended herself.

152
00:10:34,665 --> 00:10:36,505
But today, she has to face it all

153
00:10:36,585 --> 00:10:38,665
just because of your words.

154
00:10:38,745 --> 00:10:40,745
Would things have ended up like this

155
00:10:40,825 --> 00:10:42,105
if she'd stayed out of our lives?

156
00:10:42,185 --> 00:10:43,145
Mom!

157
00:10:44,065 --> 00:10:46,265
Her coming into my life

158
00:10:46,345 --> 00:10:48,625
doesn't mean she took anything from you.

159
00:10:49,145 --> 00:10:51,105
It means I chose her.

160
00:10:55,705 --> 00:10:57,825
And you saying all of that

161
00:10:57,905 --> 00:11:00,105
didn't help protect your daughter at all.

162
00:11:02,145 --> 00:11:04,705
Instead, it hurt the person
your daughter loves.

163
00:11:11,385 --> 00:11:14,305
If you choose to keep this up,

164
00:11:15,105 --> 00:11:17,105
I'll have to decide

165
00:11:18,065 --> 00:11:19,265
who I'm going to defend.

166
00:11:22,465 --> 00:11:24,145
Runch, Runch!

167
00:11:24,225 --> 00:11:26,985
Runch! Runch!

168
00:11:30,945 --> 00:11:32,345
Runch…

169
00:11:55,585 --> 00:11:56,385
Neen,

170
00:11:57,505 --> 00:11:59,745
Did you see the news about
your mother-in-law on TV?

171
00:12:01,465 --> 00:12:03,585
It's becoming a big deal.

172
00:12:05,905 --> 00:12:07,385
I saw that it's trending.

173
00:12:08,705 --> 00:12:10,265
It's not just trending.

174
00:12:10,825 --> 00:12:14,225
The news has reached the food industry
and investors too.

175
00:12:16,945 --> 00:12:19,465
I'm worried it'll affect your reputation.

176
00:12:19,545 --> 00:12:21,425
And the restaurant you're opening

177
00:12:21,505 --> 00:12:23,145
will be affected too.

178
00:12:26,385 --> 00:12:27,625
As your brother,

179
00:12:28,345 --> 00:12:31,145
I'll be honest with you.
You need to do something.

180
00:12:32,585 --> 00:12:36,505
But if I say anything now,
it'll only look like I'm making excuses.

181
00:12:37,385 --> 00:12:38,865
But if you stay quiet,

182
00:12:38,945 --> 00:12:40,905
it'll seem like
you're admitting it's true.

183
00:12:42,065 --> 00:12:44,425
I get it, but this kind of story
only stays trending

184
00:12:44,505 --> 00:12:45,865
when people get emotional.

185
00:12:45,945 --> 00:12:48,985
The more I respond,
the more it'll spread like wildfire.

186
00:12:50,145 --> 00:12:51,785
People won't listen to reason.

187
00:12:51,865 --> 00:12:54,425
They'll only side with
whoever seems more like the victim.

188
00:12:54,505 --> 00:12:57,225
So, I figured I'd just stay quiet
until the news

189
00:12:57,305 --> 00:12:59,145
eventually dies down.

190
00:13:00,105 --> 00:13:02,105
I understand where you're coming from.

191
00:13:02,905 --> 00:13:05,265
But I have to protect
our family's business too.

192
00:13:06,865 --> 00:13:08,305
I understand.

193
00:13:09,145 --> 00:13:12,025
Fine. If something happens,
I'll take responsibility for it.

194
00:13:13,025 --> 00:13:14,705
You sure you can do that?

195
00:13:15,825 --> 00:13:18,105
Yeah. I am.

196
00:13:19,505 --> 00:13:23,425
I have news about Peeracha the socialite
and her wife.

197
00:13:23,505 --> 00:13:25,465
Surely this story
will get your show's rating

198
00:13:25,545 --> 00:13:28,745
even higher than
that "Selfless Mother" video.

199
00:13:39,305 --> 00:13:40,705
Sorry I'm late.

200
00:13:42,025 --> 00:13:44,305
Let's get started, Mrs. Piyarat.

201
00:13:45,385 --> 00:13:48,865
You said your son and your daughter-in-law

202
00:13:48,945 --> 00:13:50,625
kicked you out of the house?

203
00:13:50,705 --> 00:13:52,345
Yes.

204
00:13:52,425 --> 00:13:53,865
I never thought

205
00:13:53,945 --> 00:13:57,065
that my own son would do that to me.

206
00:13:57,945 --> 00:14:00,785
He and his wife asked me
to transfer my house to them.

207
00:14:01,465 --> 00:14:05,065
He promised he'd take care of me
and never leave me.

208
00:14:05,865 --> 00:14:07,465
And I believed him.

209
00:14:09,105 --> 00:14:11,025
Once the house was in his name,

210
00:14:11,105 --> 00:14:12,865
everything changed.

211
00:14:13,985 --> 00:14:16,505
He told me it's his house,

212
00:14:17,185 --> 00:14:19,305
and I could stay

213
00:14:19,385 --> 00:14:21,385
only if I followed his rules.

214
00:14:23,625 --> 00:14:25,145
In the end,

215
00:14:25,865 --> 00:14:28,665
he kicked me out of there.

216
00:14:30,625 --> 00:14:34,945
When you signed the house over,
did you make any other agreements?

217
00:14:35,025 --> 00:14:38,545
For example, a right to live there
or any conditions regarding your care?

218
00:14:38,625 --> 00:14:40,385
Not at all.

219
00:14:41,105 --> 00:14:42,505
I only signed it over

220
00:14:42,585 --> 00:14:44,945
because I trusted
he'd be good to his mother.

221
00:14:45,705 --> 00:14:47,545
You know, some people even think

222
00:14:47,625 --> 00:14:51,185
that surely,
I pressured my own son somehow,

223
00:14:51,265 --> 00:14:53,185
so much so he kicked me out.

224
00:14:53,825 --> 00:14:58,585
But nobody asked me how I felt.

225
00:14:59,745 --> 00:15:02,425
This isn't your fault, ma'am.

226
00:15:02,505 --> 00:15:06,025
And your son and his wife
can't treat you however they want

227
00:15:06,105 --> 00:15:07,785
just because you trust him.

228
00:15:08,825 --> 00:15:12,065
We'll do our best to provide you
with legal support

229
00:15:12,145 --> 00:15:14,945
and make sure you regain your rights.

230
00:15:17,825 --> 00:15:19,625
Thank you.

231
00:15:25,905 --> 00:15:27,065
Excuse me.

232
00:15:28,425 --> 00:15:30,785
Can I talk to you for a moment?

233
00:15:33,345 --> 00:15:35,065
It's about your case.

234
00:15:36,065 --> 00:15:37,065
Sure.

235
00:15:37,745 --> 00:15:39,545
She wants a different lawyer?

236
00:15:41,785 --> 00:15:45,265
But I was just talking to Mrs. Piyarat.

237
00:15:45,345 --> 00:15:47,425
Things were going so well.

238
00:15:48,145 --> 00:15:50,185
I'm sure there's been a misunderstanding.

239
00:15:51,545 --> 00:15:52,505
There hasn't.

240
00:15:53,625 --> 00:15:56,145
She had Mr. Utt call me just a moment ago.

241
00:15:56,865 --> 00:15:57,865
Mr. Utt?

242
00:15:58,545 --> 00:15:59,785
Mrs. Piyarat

243
00:16:00,385 --> 00:16:02,785
wants Mr. Utt to handle this case
in your place.

244
00:16:06,665 --> 00:16:08,665
May I ask why?

245
00:16:08,745 --> 00:16:10,225
It's because of the news about you.

246
00:16:12,505 --> 00:16:13,545
Mrs. Piyarat is scared

247
00:16:14,465 --> 00:16:17,465
that you'll side with her son
and daughter-in-law,

248
00:16:17,545 --> 00:16:19,105
and lose her the case.

249
00:16:24,105 --> 00:16:26,265
Even though I always took her side

250
00:16:26,345 --> 00:16:28,745
for this case?

251
00:16:29,385 --> 00:16:30,505
I know.

252
00:16:31,585 --> 00:16:33,785
And I trust your professionalism.

253
00:16:35,625 --> 00:16:36,985
But some clients

254
00:16:37,785 --> 00:16:39,345
just want to be very sure.

255
00:16:42,305 --> 00:16:43,905
What about the company?

256
00:16:45,265 --> 00:16:47,585
Are you sure about me?

257
00:16:47,665 --> 00:16:49,185
If I wasn't,

258
00:16:50,305 --> 00:16:52,825
I wouldn't be speaking to you directly.

259
00:16:55,945 --> 00:16:57,545
Understood.

260
00:16:57,625 --> 00:17:01,865
I'll follow the procedure
and transfer the case to Mr. Utt.

261
00:17:03,185 --> 00:17:04,385
I'm sorry

262
00:17:05,265 --> 00:17:07,625
that your private life
is affecting your work.

263
00:17:10,145 --> 00:17:11,785
I'm not sorry.

264
00:17:12,665 --> 00:17:14,184
I'm just a bit disappointed

265
00:17:15,944 --> 00:17:18,385
that rumors hold more weight than facts.

266
00:17:30,225 --> 00:17:31,985
Here are all the files for the case.

267
00:17:35,985 --> 00:17:38,665
Please do your best in this case.

268
00:17:39,305 --> 00:17:41,105
Save Mrs. Piyarat.

269
00:17:42,385 --> 00:17:46,025
Got it. I'll do my best.

270
00:17:53,345 --> 00:17:55,145
I'm sorry, Boss.

271
00:17:56,105 --> 00:17:57,425
For what?

272
00:17:59,265 --> 00:18:01,305
I'm feeling as if

273
00:18:01,905 --> 00:18:04,265
I'm taking your work away from you.

274
00:18:09,225 --> 00:18:10,825
There's no need to apologize.

275
00:18:12,385 --> 00:18:15,425
It's up to the client to decide
who they're comfortable with.

276
00:18:16,185 --> 00:18:19,625
A lawyer's job is to build
the strongest case,

277
00:18:20,825 --> 00:18:22,945
not to keep all the work for themselves.

278
00:18:24,865 --> 00:18:27,345
I hope you won't disappoint the client.

279
00:18:33,945 --> 00:18:34,865
Here.

280
00:18:40,265 --> 00:18:41,825
Did you order anything yet?

281
00:18:41,905 --> 00:18:43,385
I was waiting for you to do it.

282
00:18:43,465 --> 00:18:44,625
Sure.

283
00:18:45,985 --> 00:18:47,825
Can we get a menu?

284
00:18:47,905 --> 00:18:50,585
Isn't that the girl in the news?

285
00:18:51,265 --> 00:18:52,945
Yeah. She chose her wife over her mom.

286
00:18:53,945 --> 00:18:57,625
There's been a new update. Apparently,

287
00:18:57,705 --> 00:18:59,025
it's because her wife is richer.

288
00:18:59,105 --> 00:19:00,505
So she's a gold-digger.

289
00:19:03,905 --> 00:19:04,945
Neen.

290
00:19:05,945 --> 00:19:06,985
No.

291
00:19:08,585 --> 00:19:11,585
Leave them be. Let's eat somewhere else.

292
00:19:16,225 --> 00:19:17,265
Fine.

293
00:19:18,025 --> 00:19:18,865
‎Let's go.

294
00:19:23,985 --> 00:19:27,425
Look. They must feel embarrassed.
That's why they're leaving.

295
00:19:29,545 --> 00:19:31,745
-Famous people, huh?
-Hey, just eat.

296
00:19:41,265 --> 00:19:42,385
Excuse me.

297
00:19:43,265 --> 00:19:45,145
If you keep talking that way,

298
00:19:45,225 --> 00:19:47,305
then let me make this clear.

299
00:19:47,865 --> 00:19:51,585
You can expect a court summons
for defamation.

300
00:20:05,945 --> 00:20:08,625
I'm sorry I killed the vibe.

301
00:20:09,345 --> 00:20:12,385
We went from a nice restaurant
to instant noodles at home.

302
00:20:13,265 --> 00:20:16,385
It's okay. The noodles are great too.

303
00:20:17,905 --> 00:20:18,745
Hey,

304
00:20:19,305 --> 00:20:22,265
you were a total badass, by the way.

305
00:20:22,985 --> 00:20:24,225
How so?

306
00:20:24,305 --> 00:20:25,505
Well, it was when you said,

307
00:20:25,585 --> 00:20:27,785
"Keep talking and expect a court summons."

308
00:20:32,425 --> 00:20:34,345
You're still in the mood to laugh?

309
00:20:38,025 --> 00:20:39,025
Of course.

310
00:20:39,985 --> 00:20:41,745
It's just gossip.

311
00:20:41,825 --> 00:20:43,385
I don't let it get to me.

312
00:20:43,465 --> 00:20:44,825
It's nonsense.

313
00:20:49,105 --> 00:20:51,105
But I don't think…

314
00:20:51,185 --> 00:20:54,145
-Yeah?
-…we should let it slide,

315
00:20:54,905 --> 00:20:57,465
especially now that there are
lots of malicious people

316
00:20:57,545 --> 00:20:59,905
who spread fake news about us.

317
00:21:02,665 --> 00:21:05,425
So what are you going to do, Runch?

318
00:21:09,745 --> 00:21:11,825
I don't want to respond emotionally.

319
00:21:12,665 --> 00:21:15,905
I don't want you
to explain yourself either.

320
00:21:18,905 --> 00:21:22,865
And I definitely won't let anyone
twist the facts about our family

321
00:21:23,505 --> 00:21:25,945
and use them against us.

322
00:21:36,905 --> 00:21:38,505
-You want more?
-No.

323
00:21:41,545 --> 00:21:43,585
YOU CAN EARN M POINTS - SCAN YOUR RECEIPTS
OR TELL THE CASHIER YOUR M CARD NUMBER

324
00:21:45,505 --> 00:21:48,025
-Are you ready?
-Yes.

325
00:22:00,145 --> 00:22:03,425
<i>I was never angry</i>
<i>or hateful toward anyone.</i>

326
00:22:05,825 --> 00:22:07,705
<i>I just want her to know that</i>

327
00:22:09,065 --> 00:22:11,105
<i>loving someone</i>

328
00:22:13,265 --> 00:22:15,025
<i>shouldn't come at the cost</i>

329
00:22:15,665 --> 00:22:17,505
<i>of breaking…</i>

330
00:22:18,305 --> 00:22:19,705
<i>a mother's heart.</i>

331
00:22:19,785 --> 00:22:23,065
What we saw was part
of Mrs. Gingkamol's interview.

332
00:22:23,145 --> 00:22:26,105
Today, we'd like to hear
Ms. Runchlaphat's side of the story

333
00:22:26,185 --> 00:22:28,065
as a daughter

334
00:22:28,145 --> 00:22:30,145
and a wife.

335
00:22:30,225 --> 00:22:31,065
Sure.

336
00:22:36,105 --> 00:22:38,585
My mother is a strong woman.

337
00:22:39,505 --> 00:22:41,425
And I'm her daughter.

338
00:22:45,985 --> 00:22:48,585
I grew up under a lot of expectations.

339
00:22:49,265 --> 00:22:51,145
I kept hearing, "You must be great."

340
00:22:51,785 --> 00:22:52,825
"You must be capable."

341
00:22:54,225 --> 00:22:56,025
"You must not let your mother down."

342
00:22:56,585 --> 00:22:58,665
<i>That very strength</i>

343
00:22:59,785 --> 00:23:02,105
<i>has made me who I am today,</i>

344
00:23:03,265 --> 00:23:05,985
<i>and I never denied that fact.</i>

345
00:23:07,465 --> 00:23:10,465
All my life, I've been trying
to overcome the expectations,

346
00:23:12,185 --> 00:23:13,745
to overcome the fear

347
00:23:14,385 --> 00:23:17,905
<i>that if one day,</i>
<i>I decide to choose my own life,</i>

348
00:23:18,585 --> 00:23:21,065
<i>I'll become a bad daughter.</i>

349
00:23:21,705 --> 00:23:24,025
Today, I've decided to choose love.

350
00:23:24,105 --> 00:23:27,745
<i>I know full well I must prove,</i>
<i>more than anyone,</i>

351
00:23:27,825 --> 00:23:31,865
<i>that I don't love her</i>
<i>because of her money.</i>

352
00:23:32,825 --> 00:23:34,585
<i>And I must prove</i>

353
00:23:35,225 --> 00:23:37,145
that I haven't left anyone behind.

354
00:23:40,305 --> 00:23:42,225
My wife and I

355
00:23:42,305 --> 00:23:45,065
have chosen to build a life together

356
00:23:45,145 --> 00:23:46,865
based on honesty

357
00:23:47,865 --> 00:23:49,985
and mutual responsibility.

358
00:23:51,385 --> 00:23:55,345
I came here to say this today
not to win against anyone,

359
00:23:56,585 --> 00:24:00,265
but to stand firm in my own truth.

360
00:24:11,545 --> 00:24:12,705
Runch!

361
00:24:17,825 --> 00:24:20,105
You never told me
you were going on that show.

362
00:24:21,065 --> 00:24:23,625
I just wanted to handle it myself.

363
00:24:25,665 --> 00:24:27,225
You know, Runch,

364
00:24:27,305 --> 00:24:30,385
you couldn't have said it better
for us both.

365
00:24:32,105 --> 00:24:33,825
I was just telling the truth.

366
00:24:38,865 --> 00:24:41,225
I'm so proud of you.

367
00:24:45,465 --> 00:24:48,585
From now on, no matter what happens,

368
00:24:48,665 --> 00:24:51,265
I won't let you face it alone.

369
00:24:52,825 --> 00:24:54,425
Same here.

370
00:24:54,505 --> 00:24:58,065
From now on, no matter what we face,
we won't let go of each other's hands.

371
00:25:00,505 --> 00:25:02,265
I have a reward for you.

372
00:25:03,905 --> 00:25:05,465
Right now?

373
00:25:06,505 --> 00:25:08,985
I guarantee you, it'll be yummy.

374
00:25:09,705 --> 00:25:11,345
Yummy, you say?

375
00:25:13,425 --> 00:25:14,465
Come on.

376
00:25:25,945 --> 00:25:28,425
This is what you meant by yummy?

377
00:25:29,265 --> 00:25:30,305
Yes.

378
00:25:37,505 --> 00:25:40,305
It looks really good. Don't you want it?

379
00:25:57,105 --> 00:25:59,785
-So good.
-Yeah.

380
00:26:10,545 --> 00:26:11,745
So yummy.

381
00:26:16,345 --> 00:26:19,905
This is the first time
it truly feels like we're on vacation.

382
00:26:21,505 --> 00:26:24,745
It's the first time
I don't have to feel guilty

383
00:26:24,825 --> 00:26:26,865
about not answering any calls.

384
00:26:30,025 --> 00:26:33,705
No checking the news, turning on the TV,
or going on social media.

385
00:26:35,145 --> 00:26:37,185
Just us spending time together.

386
00:26:43,265 --> 00:26:46,425
This house used to feel
like a battlefield, didn't it?

387
00:26:48,145 --> 00:26:49,425
Yeah.

388
00:26:51,065 --> 00:26:55,145
But today, I want it
to really feel like our home.

389
00:26:56,785 --> 00:27:00,065
Then, let's not compete with anyone today.

390
00:27:00,745 --> 00:27:04,545
There's no need to compete with anyone
or prove anything.

391
00:27:04,625 --> 00:27:06,905
All we do is rest.

392
00:28:35,585 --> 00:28:37,785
All done!

393
00:28:37,865 --> 00:28:38,785
So hot.

394
00:28:47,785 --> 00:28:49,985
-Looks pretty clean to me.
-Yeah.

395
00:28:58,305 --> 00:28:59,825
Where's Runch?

396
00:29:00,385 --> 00:29:03,465
Go get her for me now!

397
00:29:05,705 --> 00:29:06,985
What is it, Mom?

398
00:29:07,585 --> 00:29:10,185
You turned off your phone.
Didn't want me to call you or what?

399
00:29:11,665 --> 00:29:13,145
We need to talk.

400
00:29:15,985 --> 00:29:17,625
Runch and I.

401
00:29:18,305 --> 00:29:20,025
Just the two of us.

402
00:29:43,385 --> 00:29:45,825
You think what you did was right?

403
00:29:48,105 --> 00:29:51,065
You went on that show and spoke on TV.

404
00:29:51,145 --> 00:29:53,465
You made it seem like I hurt others,

405
00:29:53,545 --> 00:29:55,905
and I'm the only one who's at fault.

406
00:29:56,505 --> 00:29:58,625
Well, you went on that show earlier too.

407
00:29:59,385 --> 00:30:02,545
That's different. I was there as a mother.

408
00:30:03,145 --> 00:30:06,625
I have the right to express my feelings.
I didn't mention any names.

409
00:30:06,705 --> 00:30:09,025
People just took it the wrong way.

410
00:30:10,065 --> 00:30:10,905
Sure.

411
00:30:11,945 --> 00:30:14,665
They took it the wrong way,

412
00:30:15,225 --> 00:30:16,425
as you said.

413
00:30:16,505 --> 00:30:18,945
Are you talking back to me?

414
00:30:19,545 --> 00:30:21,265
I'm not.

415
00:30:22,225 --> 00:30:26,185
I'm just giving you
a taste of your own medicine.

416
00:30:27,985 --> 00:30:29,505
What are you talking about?

417
00:30:29,585 --> 00:30:32,065
You made the whole country
feel sorry for you.

418
00:30:32,145 --> 00:30:34,545
What about me? Who am I?

419
00:30:35,185 --> 00:30:38,145
Now I'm the cruel mother,
the selfish mother.

420
00:30:38,225 --> 00:30:40,825
I've become a villain
in my daughter's life!

421
00:30:40,905 --> 00:30:44,545
When you gave the interview, you knew
exactly how the viewers would think.

422
00:30:45,145 --> 00:30:47,185
You just chose not to take responsibility.

423
00:30:47,265 --> 00:30:49,025
I'm not taking responsibility
for anything!

424
00:30:50,905 --> 00:30:53,905
I'm a mother. I can get hurt.

425
00:30:53,985 --> 00:30:57,065
I can get sad. Can't I say anything?

426
00:30:57,145 --> 00:30:58,625
You can.

427
00:30:59,985 --> 00:31:02,745
But Neen paid the price, not you.

428
00:31:03,425 --> 00:31:06,785
Our lives were ruined
because of that woman.

429
00:31:08,705 --> 00:31:12,825
Before, I never
had to give any interviews.

430
00:31:12,905 --> 00:31:16,785
I never had to feel embarrassed
or cry on TV for anyone's entertainment.

431
00:31:17,385 --> 00:31:19,265
Don't let her hear that.

432
00:31:19,345 --> 00:31:22,665
What, are you afraid she'll be upset?
What about me, then?

433
00:31:22,745 --> 00:31:24,745
Can I be upset?

434
00:31:24,825 --> 00:31:26,185
Can I feel hurt?

435
00:31:27,465 --> 00:31:29,825
Or do I have to be the only one
who's understanding?

436
00:31:34,465 --> 00:31:35,665
Don't forget.

437
00:31:37,145 --> 00:31:38,865
You started it.

438
00:31:40,025 --> 00:31:42,265
So don't blame me.

439
00:31:45,225 --> 00:31:47,105
So you really chose her.

440
00:31:49,505 --> 00:31:51,745
You really chose her over me.

441
00:31:58,745 --> 00:32:00,505
I chose my own life.

442
00:32:01,705 --> 00:32:04,825
And I won't let anyone
hurt the one I love.

443
00:32:08,865 --> 00:32:10,305
No one.

444
00:32:15,785 --> 00:32:17,145
So from now on,

445
00:32:18,065 --> 00:32:19,865
what am I to you?

446
00:32:23,665 --> 00:32:24,625
Am I…

447
00:32:25,905 --> 00:32:29,225
not the one you love anymore?

448
00:32:55,865 --> 00:32:57,665
You're still my mother.

449
00:32:59,905 --> 00:33:01,665
I love you, Mom.

450
00:33:07,745 --> 00:33:09,665
But there should be boundaries

451
00:33:10,705 --> 00:33:12,425
in our relationship,

452
00:33:14,865 --> 00:33:18,105
like we're two adults
who respect each other's privacy.

453
00:33:22,825 --> 00:33:26,385
Boundaries? Don't sugarcoat it.

454
00:33:30,945 --> 00:33:34,625
In reality, what you're trying to say is…

455
00:33:37,865 --> 00:33:39,105
"From now on,

456
00:33:41,025 --> 00:33:43,985
stay the hell out of my life."

457
00:33:44,065 --> 00:33:45,225
Isn't that right?

458
00:33:46,585 --> 00:33:48,665
Well, if it's not really necessary

459
00:33:50,185 --> 00:33:52,105
or a matter of life and death,

460
00:33:55,905 --> 00:33:58,065
then there's no need for you to see me.

461
00:34:31,465 --> 00:34:34,585
You don't have to say anything.
I heard everything.

462
00:35:02,745 --> 00:35:04,865
We're alone together now.

463
00:35:07,185 --> 00:35:09,545
You don't have to try to be strong.

464
00:35:25,505 --> 00:35:26,425
Yeah?

465
00:35:38,505 --> 00:35:40,465
I wasn't dragged into this.

466
00:35:41,705 --> 00:35:43,345
I chose this.

467
00:35:45,785 --> 00:35:49,185
I chose you. I chose us.

468
00:35:55,865 --> 00:35:57,665
If today was tiring,

469
00:35:58,865 --> 00:36:01,065
we can be tired together.

470
00:36:01,145 --> 00:36:03,385
It's okay to win at nothing for one day.

471
00:36:16,305 --> 00:36:17,985
I feel so lucky…

472
00:36:20,065 --> 00:36:22,145
to have you by my side.

473
00:36:25,945 --> 00:36:28,425
Then how about you let me
stay by your side forever?

474
00:37:10,225 --> 00:37:11,905
Did you get any sleep last night?

475
00:37:14,185 --> 00:37:15,345
I did.

476
00:37:16,745 --> 00:37:19,625
I did because you were there by my side.

477
00:37:27,625 --> 00:37:29,305
Penny for your thoughts?

478
00:37:35,985 --> 00:37:38,145
I'm deciding

479
00:37:38,785 --> 00:37:42,185
whether we should leave
what happened as a wound

480
00:37:42,825 --> 00:37:46,745
or change it to something better.

481
00:37:50,105 --> 00:37:53,785
I want to start a small project.
Something low-key.

482
00:37:53,865 --> 00:37:56,345
It doesn't have to be a big deal.

483
00:37:56,425 --> 00:37:58,985
Maybe a foundation for children

484
00:37:59,785 --> 00:38:01,705
or women

485
00:38:01,785 --> 00:38:03,945
who are rejected by their families

486
00:38:04,625 --> 00:38:07,065
just for being themselves

487
00:38:07,145 --> 00:38:09,025
or because of their gender.

488
00:38:10,865 --> 00:38:17,185
I don't want anyone to feel
like their love is a crime.

489
00:38:19,865 --> 00:38:23,105
That way, our love
won't stay just between us,

490
00:38:23,985 --> 00:38:27,145
but we'll get to give our love
to others too.

491
00:38:28,385 --> 00:38:31,585
I don't know how well I'll do it.

492
00:38:32,705 --> 00:38:35,465
I just know I don't want to do it alone.

493
00:38:38,225 --> 00:38:40,825
Well, have I ever let you?

494
00:38:44,425 --> 00:38:46,905
If the world is cruel to us,

495
00:38:46,985 --> 00:38:49,785
we just have to be kind in return.
That's all.

496
00:38:52,465 --> 00:38:55,465
How about this? We'll ask Nai for advice

497
00:38:55,545 --> 00:38:57,025
about the foundation.

498
00:38:59,145 --> 00:39:00,825
Sounds good.

499
00:39:00,905 --> 00:39:03,465
I'm sure he'd be a big help.

500
00:39:09,585 --> 00:39:11,145
Absolutely.

501
00:39:12,185 --> 00:39:15,585
Our company already owns
a foundation for children in need.

502
00:39:15,665 --> 00:39:18,105
We already have
the infrastructure in place,

503
00:39:18,185 --> 00:39:20,385
and our operations are transparent.

504
00:39:22,785 --> 00:39:26,785
Some of the families we've worked with
faced the same issue.

505
00:39:27,705 --> 00:39:29,585
Some children don't lack money.

506
00:39:29,665 --> 00:39:31,385
They lack a place where they belong.

507
00:39:32,705 --> 00:39:35,105
If you want to start a foundation,

508
00:39:35,905 --> 00:39:37,705
it could be a safe space for them.

509
00:39:39,065 --> 00:39:41,265
A place where no one judges them.

510
00:39:41,985 --> 00:39:43,105
Yeah.

511
00:39:43,185 --> 00:39:45,025
I don't want anyone to feel

512
00:39:45,105 --> 00:39:46,985
like they don't belong anywhere.

513
00:39:48,905 --> 00:39:51,665
I want to make sure
everything's done properly.

514
00:39:51,745 --> 00:39:53,705
I don't want anyone to get hurt,

515
00:39:53,785 --> 00:39:55,745
including their families.

516
00:39:57,745 --> 00:39:59,185
My thoughts exactly.

517
00:40:30,905 --> 00:40:32,505
-Hello.
-Hello, ma'am.

518
00:40:32,585 --> 00:40:35,065
You work here, right?

519
00:40:35,145 --> 00:40:36,145
Yes.

520
00:40:37,145 --> 00:40:38,945
You're my boss's mother, right?

521
00:40:39,665 --> 00:40:41,345
I work for her.

522
00:40:42,665 --> 00:40:44,305
You recognize me?

523
00:40:44,385 --> 00:40:45,705
Of course I do.

524
00:40:45,785 --> 00:40:48,225
I just watched the show
where you gave the interview.

525
00:40:50,705 --> 00:40:52,585
I'm on your side, by the way.

526
00:40:54,105 --> 00:40:56,265
Really? That's good to hear.

527
00:40:56,945 --> 00:41:00,225
Oh, right.
I bought some food for everyone,

528
00:41:00,305 --> 00:41:02,345
but I don't want to bother Runch.

529
00:41:02,425 --> 00:41:03,585
Can you hand it out for me?

530
00:41:03,665 --> 00:41:04,505
Sure.

531
00:41:04,585 --> 00:41:09,065
And please don't tell Runch I came here.

532
00:41:09,865 --> 00:41:10,985
Why not?

533
00:41:14,745 --> 00:41:16,625
I just don't want her
to feel uncomfortable.

534
00:41:20,065 --> 00:41:23,145
It's because of the interview
my boss recently gave, right?

535
00:41:23,225 --> 00:41:25,625
That's why you don't want anyone
to know you're here.

536
00:41:35,585 --> 00:41:37,105
It's alright.

537
00:41:38,665 --> 00:41:40,585
I never thought

538
00:41:40,665 --> 00:41:43,505
my daughter could be so mad at me.

539
00:41:47,185 --> 00:41:49,585
She's always taking her wife's side,

540
00:41:50,105 --> 00:41:52,425
like I'm not her mother anymore.

541
00:41:52,945 --> 00:41:55,865
Like I'm an outsider
in my own daughter's life.

542
00:42:06,945 --> 00:42:08,985
It hurts me so bad.

543
00:42:09,865 --> 00:42:11,745
It really does.

544
00:42:13,185 --> 00:42:14,945
Everything I did

545
00:42:15,945 --> 00:42:17,265
was for my daughter.

546
00:42:18,065 --> 00:42:20,345
Never for myself.

547
00:42:23,985 --> 00:42:25,865
I understand.

548
00:42:26,505 --> 00:42:30,545
To a mother, this is something
that hurts deeply.

549
00:42:33,185 --> 00:42:36,305
I just didn't want her
to have a difficult life,

550
00:42:37,145 --> 00:42:40,505
but in the end,
I'm the one who's at fault.

551
00:42:50,465 --> 00:42:52,145
I've known her for so long.

552
00:42:53,425 --> 00:42:56,745
She only changed when this person
came into her life.

553
00:43:05,105 --> 00:43:08,665
Let me know
if I can help you with anything.

554
00:43:08,745 --> 00:43:10,305
I'm on your side.

555
00:43:15,705 --> 00:43:16,785
In that case,

556
00:43:17,865 --> 00:43:19,305
can I get your number?

557
00:43:20,625 --> 00:43:21,705
Of course.

558
00:43:23,705 --> 00:43:24,745
I'm Utt, by the way.

559
00:43:26,065 --> 00:43:27,665
I really appreciate it, Utt.

560
00:43:28,265 --> 00:43:32,225
At least some people still listen to me.

561
00:44:08,665 --> 00:44:10,305
What about you, Ms. Runchlaphat?

562
00:44:10,385 --> 00:44:12,025
What do you like about Ms. Peeracha?

563
00:44:12,105 --> 00:44:13,345
1 YEAR AGO

564
00:44:17,145 --> 00:44:20,985
She's very… truthful.

565
00:44:22,745 --> 00:44:24,865
She stays true to her feelings,

566
00:44:24,945 --> 00:44:26,465
to others…

567
00:44:28,425 --> 00:44:31,505
and also to the feeling of love.

568
00:44:33,065 --> 00:44:34,305
At work,

569
00:44:34,905 --> 00:44:37,025
I've met people who are eloquent,

570
00:44:37,705 --> 00:44:39,825
people who are confident,

571
00:44:41,065 --> 00:44:44,185
and lots of people who are skilled.

572
00:44:45,305 --> 00:44:47,745
But Neen is the only one

573
00:44:49,385 --> 00:44:52,025
who's not afraid to say,
"I can't take it."

574
00:44:58,905 --> 00:45:03,265
And she doesn't say it
to ask for anything.

575
00:45:04,585 --> 00:45:09,265
She only says it
to let me know she really can't take it.

576
00:45:12,825 --> 00:45:14,425
I like how she doesn't

577
00:45:15,265 --> 00:45:16,825
try to beat anyone,

578
00:45:18,505 --> 00:45:22,305
but rather, she tries
to be honest with herself.

579
00:45:24,585 --> 00:45:26,945
And so, she taught me that

580
00:45:28,105 --> 00:45:30,465
love isn't about arguments

581
00:45:32,345 --> 00:45:36,425
or proving who's right.

582
00:45:37,785 --> 00:45:39,505
It's about choosing.

583
00:45:40,105 --> 00:45:42,185
Choosing to stay by each other's side,

584
00:45:43,305 --> 00:45:45,785
even when nothing is clear.

585
00:45:53,625 --> 00:45:55,385
That's why I chose Neen.

586
00:45:57,425 --> 00:46:00,505
Not because you are perfect,

587
00:46:02,545 --> 00:46:04,505
but because

588
00:46:05,585 --> 00:46:07,585
you are the truth

589
00:46:08,865 --> 00:46:11,985
I want to protect for the rest of my life.

590
00:46:47,305 --> 00:46:48,865
I did everything for you.

591
00:46:48,945 --> 00:46:53,065
<i>But in the end, I wasn't the one you chose</i>
<i>to stand by.</i>

592
00:46:53,145 --> 00:46:54,345
Runch is done with you.

593
00:46:54,425 --> 00:46:57,305
If she's really
going to let her wife bully me,

594
00:46:57,985 --> 00:46:59,225
then so be it.

595
00:46:59,305 --> 00:47:01,785
To our family. To us.

596
00:47:05,105 --> 00:47:06,425
Crazy bitch!

597
00:47:06,505 --> 00:47:08,105
-You bitch, how dare you!
-Stop it!

598
00:47:08,185 --> 00:47:09,945
You had no right to do this to me!

599
00:47:55,465 --> 00:47:57,465
Subtitle translation by:
Ramil Natnitiwitaya

